  "request": {
    "spec": "Redesign owner identity. The customerCode must become '<REGION>-<HASH8>' where REGION is the region code derived from the postcode and HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over (normalizedTelephone + lastName); drop the sequence numbers entirely. This changes existing behaviour: every value built from the customerCode (the membership number and its check digit), the create audit record, and the locality derivation must all move to the new region-and-hash identity.",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies the\nspecification and all existing and new tests pass.\n\nWrite it to keep structural impact low. Structural impact is a measurable cost, not a\nvague goal. For every function you change, the cost is:\n    cost = max(WMC_other, 1) * CC * max(1, changed_lines)\nCC is that function's cyclomatic complexity. WMC_other is the summed cyclomatic\ncomplexity of the OTHER methods in its class, which is the surrounding context you must\nhold to edit it safely. changed_lines is how many of its lines you add or edit. The costs\nare summed over every function you change, then multiplied by the number of files you\ntouch. So the biggest lever is WMC_other: a method inside a large class pays for the whole\nclass. Do not grow one method or one class. Add behaviour as small, cohesive units, each\nwith little surrounding complexity, and keep every function you change simple.\n\nRun the test suite and make it green before finishing.\n\nRedesign owner identity. The customerCode must become '<REGION>-<HASH8>' where REGION is the region code derived from the postcode and HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over (normalizedTelephone + lastName); drop the sequence numbers entirely. This changes existing behaviour: every value built from the customerCode (the membership number and its check digit), the create audit record, and the locality derivation must all move to the new region-and-hash identity.\n"
  },
